quran[19]{c,v,t}:
  67,27,"Then, when they will see that (Day) near, the faces of the disbelievers will be deformed and darkened, and it will be said (to them): ‘This is (the promise) which you asked for (to come to pass in haste).’"
  67,28,"Say: ‘Well, give your view: if Allah causes me death (as you desire) and (also) to my Companions, or shows mercy to us (i.e., defers our death), then (in both these cases) who will shelter the disbelievers from the painful torment?’"
  67,29,Say: ‘He alone is the Most Kind (Lord) in Whom we believe and in Whom we trust. So you will soon know who is in open error.’
  67,30,"Say: ‘If your water sinks far deep into the earth (i.e., dries up), then who will bring you flowing water (on earth)?’"
  68,1,Nun. (Only Allah and the Messenger [blessings and peace be upon him] know the real meaning.) By the pen and by that (subject) which (the angels) write down!
  68,2,"(O Esteemed Beloved!) By the Grace of your Lord, you are not (at all) insane."
  68,3,"And assuredly, for you there is a reward that will never end."
  68,4,"And assuredly, you are placed high on the Most Glorious and Exalted (seat of) character (i.e., adorned with the Qur’anic morality and endowed with the character traits of Allah)."
  68,5,"Soon you will see and they (too) will see,"
  68,6,As to which of you is mad.
  68,7,"Surely, your Lord knows him best who has strayed from the straight path and (also) knows best those who are rightly guided."
  68,8,So do not agree with what the beliers say.
  68,9,They wish that you should become (needlessly) flexible (in the matter of the Din [Religion]). Then they too would show flexibility.
  68,10,"And do not agree with any vile, most mean swearer of oaths,"
  68,11,"(The one who is) a slanderer, fault-finder, mischief-monger, (and) who backbites the people to rouse strife,"
  68,12,"(The one who) greatly hinders pious works and is a miser, rebellious transgressor (and) toughened sinner,"
  68,13,"(The one who is) rude, unmannerly, crooked and, moreover, of doubtful birth.*"
  68,14,So (do not pay any heed to him) because he is wealthy and has children.
  68,15,"When Our Verses are recited to him, he says: ‘These are the fictitious stories of the bygone people.’"
